  "status": "baseline",
  "created": "2026-09-29",
  "taxonomy_version": "taxonomy-v2",
  "description": "Rules-only baseline for taxonomy v2 (frontier-lab harm areas). Written from the framework's severity table plus lessons carried over from the archived v1 experiment (refusals are working safeguards; narrow 'assistant provided' phrases; low confidence must not lower severity; P3 without a specialist category goes to Support). Written BEFORE the v2 evaluation dataset existed and before any v2 evaluation was run. Severe-harm areas (CBRN, child safety, self-harm, violent extremism) are detected from structured policy fields in classifier output and specialist review notes (policy_area=..., content_provided=yes/no) because their content is held in a restricted evidence store and never described in the ticket. Keyword lexicons plus structured intake fields; first matching severity rule wins.",
